text that links to the C++ method that is actually called.

Go through every annotation to see how it affects the Python API from the
user's perspective.

Generate a standard description for copy ctors.

Enums implemented as Python enums (ie. C++ scoped enums) should be documented
as such.

Consider identifying methods that are virtual or protected.

Handle namespace extenders.

Handle slot extenders.

Handle opaque classes.

Handle :platform:.  The issue is that we do not have user friendly names in the
.sip file.  Also it needs to be tied in with sip's %Feature directive.

When no modules are specified on the command line search the sip root directory
(with standard exclusions, eg. QScintilla).
